     "label": "Atoms",
     "x": 22,
     "y": 28,
     "color": "#2563eb",
     "html": "The tiny particles matter is made of.",
     "why": "Suggested by Democritus (5th century BC); proved by experiments by John Dalton (1808), who noticed that substances always combine in fixed proportions. In 1905 Albert Einstein explained the random movement of pollen grains in water (Brownian motion) as the effect of the collisions of molecules: it was the proof that they really exist."
